  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dregs', '/dreɡz/', 'n.', 'Cặn bã, phần thừa thãi vô giá trị', 'By the winter of 1777, the besieged garrison had consumed their reserves and were reduced to drinking the foul dregs of stagnant cisterns.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 73),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'drivel', '/ˈdrɪvl/', 'n.', 'Chuyện nhảm nhí, lời nói vô nghĩa', 'The eminent philosopher refused to dignify the sensationalist pamphlet with a rebuttal, dismissing its conspiracy theories as unlettered drivel.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 74),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'droll', '/drəʊl/', 'adj.', 'Khôi hài, hóm hỉnh kỳ quặc', 'With dry wit and deadpan delivery, the satirical columnist offered a droll commentary on the absurdities of metropolitan high society.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 75),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'drone', '/drəʊn/', 'v.', 'Nói giọng đều đều buồn ngủ, kêu vo ve', 'As the parliamentary clerk continued to drone through the dozens of technical amendments, several legislators quietly dozed in their benches.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 76),
