  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'drudgery', '/ˈdrʌdʒəri/', 'n.', 'Công việc cực nhọc, sự vất vả nhàm chán', 'Prior to the mechanization of agriculture, weeding sprawling cotton fields by hand represented an unremitting drudgery for farm laborers.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 78),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dubious', '/ˈdjuːbiəs/', 'adj.', 'Đáng nghi, mơ hồ, hoài nghi', 'Independent economic analysts remained deeply dubious of the central bank''s inflation forecast, citing volatile global commodity prices.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 79),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'ductile', '/ˈdʌktaɪl/', 'adj.', 'Dễ uốn, dễ dát mỏng, dễ uốn nắn', 'Because gold is exceptionally ductile, a single ounce can be drawn into an ultrafine wire extending over fifty miles without fracturing.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 80),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dulcet', '/ˈdʌlsɪt/', 'adj.', 'Êm dịu, ngọt ngào, thánh thót', 'The contralto''s dulcet voice resonated through the stone amphitheater, soothing the tense crowd gathered in the piazza.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 81),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dumbfound', '/dʌmˈfaʊnd/', 'v.', 'Làm chết lặng, làm sửng sốt', 'The astronomer''s revelation that the distant galaxy exhibited impossible orbital mechanics served to dumbfound the astrophysics community.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 82),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dupe', '/djuːp/', 'v.', 'Lừa gạt, đánh lừa', 'By forging official government seals and falsifying deeds, the con artist managed to dupe unsuspecting investors into funding fictitious railroad lines.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 83),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'duplicity', '/djuːˈplɪsəti/', 'n.', 'Tính hai lòng, sự xảo trá', 'The declassified memos exposed the cabinet minister''s duplicity, showing that he secretly courted foreign monopolists while publicly decrying their predatory practices.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 84),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'duration', '/djuˈreɪʃn/', 'n.', 'Thời lượng, khoảng thời gian tồn tại', 'Because the polar night extends for the entire duration of the arctic winter, expedition members must cope with relentless psychological strain.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 85),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'duress', '/djuˈres/', 'n.', 'Sự ép buộc, sự cưỡng ép', 'The tribunal nullified the treaty after uncovering evidence that the sovereign had signed under physical duress and imminent threat of bombardment.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 86),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dutiful', '/ˈdjuːtɪfl/', 'adj.', 'Tận tụy, làm tròn bổn phận, biết vâng lời', 'Throughout four decades of turbulent naval service, the admiral remained a dutiful commander who placed constitutional loyalty above political ambition.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 87),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dwarf', '/dwɔːf/', 'v.', 'Làm lu mờ, thu nhỏ lại khi so sánh', 'The staggering scale of the transcontinental railway project threatened to dwarf all previous civil engineering achievements in the nation''s history.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 88),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dwindle', '/ˈdwɪndl/', 'v.', 'Thu hẹp dần, cạn kiệt dần, suy giảm', 'As annual rainfall plummeted and aquifer levels dropped, municipal water reserves began to dwindle to precarious thresholds.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 89),
  ('e8f7c92b-8a1e-4c3d-b5e2-0a1b2c3d4e5f', 'dynamic', '/daɪˈnæmɪk/', 'adj.', 'Năng động, luôn biến đổi, năng tiến', 'Ecologists increasingly conceptualize estuaries as dynamic transitional biomes whose species diversity depends on continuous tidal fluctuations.', 'Lesson 10', 10, 90),
